 "what": "a place of the span store names, under held, the rows it holds back under «only this pointing», each with why: «otherwise», a row the corpus lane grades pointed otherwise where STEP's own tags on the place's words (TAHOT's Strong's number on each word's core, its letter set aside) name no one entry over every word; «silent», a row with no pointed headword. A row graded same or same word stands, and so does one graded otherwise where STEP tags every word with one entry or a word carries no tag. Held is the place's own and never the key's: one key stands at many places. The reader leaves a held row out of the run's card at that place under «only» and counts it (pointed otherwise with the pointing's withheld, no pointing apart); under «keep» and «letters» it stands. A place that holds none carries no held; every other member of a place and every row is the lane's, byte for byte",
 "ruled": {
